    prompt: "A monotonic stack holds unresolved indices in a useful order; each new value resolves the candidates it dominates.\n\nFor each position in `values`, return the nearest **previous** value that is strictly smaller than it, or `-1` when there is none.\n\n`[3, 1, 4, 2]` gives `[-1, -1, 1, 1]`. Aim for O(n) total, not O(n^2).",
