    estimatedMinutes: 15,
    prompt: "Dijkstra always finalizes the cheapest tentative distance. A vertex can sit in the heap several times, so any entry worse than the recorded distance is **stale** and must be skipped.\n\n`edges` are undirected `(u, v, weight)` with non-negative weights. Return the distance from `start` to every vertex, `-1` when unreachable.\n\n`(3, [(0, 1, 4), (0, 2, 1), (2, 1, 2)], 0)` gives `[0, 3, 1]` — via 2, not the direct edge.",
