    title: "Augment by the bottleneck",
    teaches: ["py.algo.max-flow-guided"],
    requires: [],
    difficulty: { concept: 6, implementation: 5, recall: 5 },
    estimatedMinutes: 18,
    prompt: "Edmonds-Karp repeatedly finds a shortest residual path, pushes its **bottleneck** capacity along it, and adds matching **reverse** capacity so a later path can undo the choice. It stops when no residual path remains — and that final cut is the min cut.\n\n`edges` are directed `(u, v, capacity)`. Return the maximum flow from `source` to `sink`.\n\n`(4, [(0,1,3),(0,2,2),(1,3,2),(2,3,3)], 0, 3)` gives `4`.",
    exportName: "max_flow",
    scaffolds: { L1: "from collections import deque\n\ndef max_flow(vertex_count, edges, source, sink):\n    pass", L2: "from collections import deque\n\ndef max_flow(vertex_count, edges, source, sink):\n    pass", L3: "from collections import deque\n\ndef max_flow(vertex_count, edges, source, sink):\n    pass", L4: "" },
    tests: [
      { name: "two parallel routes", code: "assert fn(4, [(0,1,3),(0,2,2),(1,3,2),(2,3,3)], 0, 3) == 4", hidden: false },
      { name: "single edge", code: "assert fn(2, [(0,1,5)], 0, 1) == 5", hidden: false },
      { name: "no path", code: "assert fn(3, [(0,1,4)], 0, 2) == 0", hidden: false },
      { name: "bottleneck limits the chain", code: "assert fn(3, [(0,1,10),(1,2,1)], 0, 2) == 1", hidden: false },
      { name: "reverse capacity allows rerouting", code: "assert fn(4, [(0,1,3),(1,2,1),(1,3,1),(2,3,3)], 0, 3) == 2", hidden: true }
    ],
    hints: [
      { rung: 0, text: "Track residual capacity in a matrix, and treat both directions as traversable." },
      { rung: 1, text: "BFS from the source using only edges with residual capacity left." },
      { rung: 2, text: "Push the path's smallest capacity, subtract it forward, and add it backward." }
    ],
    solution: "from collections import deque\n\ndef max_flow(vertex_count, edges, source, sink):\n    capacity = [[0] * vertex_count for _ in range(vertex_count)]\n    adjacency = [set() for _ in range(vertex_count)]\n    for u, v, cap in edges:\n        capacity[u][v] += cap\n        adjacency[u].add(v)\n        adjacency[v].add(u)\n    total = 0\n    while True:\n        parent = [-1] * vertex_count\n        parent[source] = source\n        queue = deque([source])\n        while queue and parent[sink] == -1:\n            vertex = queue.popleft()\n            for neighbour in adjacency[vertex]:\n                if parent[neighbour] == -1 and capacity[vertex][neighbour] > 0:\n                    parent[neighbour] = vertex\n                    queue.append(neighbour)\n        if parent[sink] == -1:\n            return total\n        bottleneck = float('inf')\n        node = sink\n        while node != source:\n            bottleneck = min(bottleneck, capacity[parent[node]][node])\n            node = parent[node]\n        node = sink\n        while node != source:\n            capacity[parent[node]][node] -= bottleneck\n            capacity[node][parent[node]] += bottleneck\n            node = parent[node]\n        total += bottleneck",
    language: "python",
