    prompt: "Span is what a set of vectors can build; independence removes redundant directions. **Rank** is how many directions genuinely survive — and it tells you whether your features carry duplicate information.\n\nReturn the rank of `matrix` using Gaussian elimination. Treat a value as zero when its absolute value is below `1e-9`.\n\n`[[1, 2], [2, 4]]` has rank `1` — the second row is just twice the first.",
