    estimatedMinutes: 12,
    prompt: "Bernoulli models one binary result; **Binomial** models the number of successes in a fixed number of independent trials.\n\nReturn `P(exactly k successes in n trials)` for success probability `p`:\n`C(n, k) * p^k * (1 - p)^(n - k)`. Return `0.0` when `k` is outside `0..n`.\n\nTwo heads in three fair flips has probability `0.375`.",
    exportName: "binomial_pmf",
    scaffolds: { L1: "import math\n\ndef binomial_pmf(n, k, p):\n    pass", L2: "import math\n\ndef binomial_pmf(n, k, p):\n    pass", L3: "import math\n\ndef binomial_pmf(n, k, p):\n    pass", L4: "" },
