    prompt: "Return whether `pattern` matches the whole of `text`. A `?` matches exactly one character and a `*` matches any run of characters, including none at all.\n\nThe state is a pair of positions. A star gives a **two-way** transition: absorb one more character of the text, or step past the star without consuming anything. Matching greedily commits to a choice the rest of the pattern may not survive.\n\nA pattern of stars alone matches the empty text.",
