    prompt: "Normalize `batch`, a list of equal-length rows, to zero mean and unit variance. When `axis` is `\"batch\"` compute the statistics down each column, across examples. When it is `\"layer\"` compute them across each row, inside one example.\n\nDivide by `sqrt(variance + eps)` so a constant row or column does not divide by zero. Return the rows rounded to six places.\n\nRaise `ValueError` for an unknown axis or an empty batch.",
