    estimatedMinutes: 15,
    prompt: "Build a table of the **smallest prime factor** of every number up to `limit`, then return `(primes, factorisations)` where `factorisations` maps each number in `queries` to a dict of prime to exponent.\n\nA number whose stored factor is itself was never crossed out, so it is prime. Each prime may start marking at its own square, because every smaller multiple already carries a smaller prime's mark.\n\nRaise `ValueError` when a query exceeds the limit or is below two.",
    exportName: "factor_table",
    scaffolds: { L1: "def factor_table(limit, queries=()):\n    pass", L2: "def factor_table(limit, queries=()):\n    pass", L3: "def factor_table(limit, queries=()):\n    pass", L4: "" },
