    prompt: "Return the count for `kind`, one of `\"permutation\"`, `\"combination\"`, `\"repeats\"` or `\"distribute\"`.\n\nPermutations count ordered selections of `k` from `n`. Combinations divide that by the orderings of the chosen items. `repeats` counts ordered selections **with repetition allowed**, which is `n` to the power `k`. `distribute` counts ways to split `k` identical items among `n` labelled groups.\n\nRaise `ValueError` for an unknown kind, a negative argument, or a selection larger than the pool where that matters.",
    exportName: "count",
    scaffolds: { L1: "from math import comb, factorial\n\ndef count(kind, n, k):\n    pass", L2: "from math import comb, factorial\n\ndef count(kind, n, k):\n    pass", L3: "from math import comb, factorial\n\ndef count(kind, n, k):\n    pass", L4: "" },
